<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>PAYE tax bands for resident individuals, from 1 July 2023 (Kenya Revenue Authority; Finance Act 2023):</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Monthly taxable pay (Ksh)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Rate</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">First <m>24\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>10\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>8333</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>25\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>467\,667</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>30\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Next <m>300\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>32.5\%</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Above <m>800\,000</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>35\%</m></cell></row></tabular><p>Personal relief: Ksh <m>2400</m> a month, taken off the tax. PAYE is never negative.</p><p>Achieng's payslip for one month shows:</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Payslip, Achieng</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Ksh</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Basic pay</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{48\,000}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Allowances</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{9000}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Pension contribution (taken off before tax)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2500}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Other deductions, in total (after tax)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{4300}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) Find the taxable pay.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) Find the PAYE.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </p><p>(c) Find the net pay.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans3"/>  </p><p>Give each answer to the nearest shilling, or exactly in cents.</p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Gross pay <m>= {48\,000} + {9000} = {57\,000}</m>. Taxable pay <m>= {57\,000} - {2500} = {54\,500}</m>.</p><p>Split Ksh <m>{54\,500}</m> into the bands:</p><ul><li>first <m>{24\,000}</m> at <m>10\%</m>: <m>{2400}</m></li><li>next <m>{8333}</m> at <m>25\%</m>: <m>{2083.25}</m></li><li>next <m>{22\,167}</m> at <m>30\%</m>: <m>{6650.10}</m></li></ul><p>Tax before relief <m>= {11\,133.35}</m>.</p><p>(b) PAYE <m>= {11\,133.35} - 2400 = {8733.35}</m>.</p><p>(c) Net pay <m>=</m> gross pay <m>-</m> pension <m>-</m> PAYE <m>-</m> other deductions <m>= {57\,000} - {2500} - {8733.35} - {4300} = {41\,466.65}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>54500</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>8733.35</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>41466.65</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>